Z||000000||DJRice||10-22-2001||11:14 PM||||Is anyone else having a problem with that stupid rotary volume control knob.  I turn the thing and sometimes the volume goes up instead of down, if it moves at all.  I guess it has a bit of corrosion it it or something.  Has anybody devised a way of cleaning this thing?<P>This is the same problem that inspired me to get rid of my Sony CD Player with its "Rotary Encoder" and buy the Delco Radio in the first place.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> <BR>"And this one time, on the Fiero Forum..."||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rick 88||10-23-2001||01:55 AM||||A friend of mine owns a car radio repair shop. He told me that the rotary volume controls are prone to failure on the late model Delco units. Apparently the control is fragile. They usually replace the control and that solves the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||10-23-2001||09:19 AM||||Both of our GTs have that radio and they do the same thing.  It is anoying but not worth spending money to fix.  <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
